# How this page reaches `typesafe-ai/jev` through the Vercel AI Gateway. Neither
# variable carries a `VITE_` prefix, deliberately: a `VITE_`-prefixed name is
# inlined into the browser bundle and handed to every visitor. Both are read
# only in Node — by the `jev-api` plugin in `vite.config.ts` for the dev and
# preview servers, and by `api/jev.ts` on Vercel.
#
# Without either, the page still works: it falls back to the local rule judge
# in `src/localJudge.ts` and says so on screen.

# --- the OIDC route: free, no card, what a Hobby account gets ---------------
# Do not write this by hand. Run, once:
#
#   vercel login
#   vercel link              # creates the project AND writes .env.local
#
# then restart the dev server. No GitHub repo and no deployment are needed:
# the Vercel project is only the identity the token is minted against, and
# `vercel link` makes one from this folder. The token lasts about twelve
# hours — `vercel env pull` refreshes it. `src/server/judge.ts` prefers
# it over an API key.
#
# VERCEL_OIDC_TOKEN=            (lives in .env.local, written by the CLI)

# --- the API-key route: bills the account that owns the key -----------------
# Only worth setting on a paid account. On an account with no card every
# request comes back 403 "AI Gateway requires a valid credit card on file",
# which looks like a bad key and is not. Keep it in `.env`, not `.env.local`,
# because `vercel env pull` overwrites the latter.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
